lorida all interchangeable unless an interview dictates otherwise. memcite\n\nI checked **September 26–29** because you haven’t locked the departure date yet. On the Expedia inventory I pulled, here’s the current baseline **per person**:\n\n| Depart LAS | Florida airport | Fare | Routing |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| **Sat 9/26** | **JAX** | **$196.26** | Frontier, 1 stop, 8h31 |\n| **Sat 9/26** | **MIA** | **$200.33** | Frontier, 1 stop, 10h08 |\n| **Sat 9/26** | **FLL** | **$200.33** | Frontier, 1 stop, 8h14 |\n| Sat 9/26 | TPA | $259.31 | Frontier, 1 stop |\n| Sat 9/26 | MCO | $268.47 | **Frontier nonstop**, 4h24 |\n| **Tue 9/29** | **JAX** | **$196.26** | Frontier, 1 stop, 8h31 |\n| **Tue 9/29** | **MIA** | **$200.33** | Frontier, 1 stop |\n| **Tue 9/29** | **FLL** | **$200.33** | Frontier, 1 stop |\n| Tue 9/29 | MCO | $257.28 | **Frontier nonstop**, 4h24 |\n| Tue 9/29 | TPA | $259.31 | Frontier, 1 stop |\n\nSo our **working number is basically $200** to get you back into Florida if we’re flexible about the airport.\n\nAnd one thing jumped out immediately: **Jacksonville absolutely belongs in this search.** On both Saturday and Tuesday it actually came in slightly under Miami/Fort Lauderdale at **$196.26**. Given the interview situation, that could be strategically useful too. memcite\n\n### The rule for this chat\n\nWe should evaluate every flight on **true exit cost**, not the headline ticket:\n\n**airfare + luggage + Florida ground transportation = actual cost to get positioned.**\n\nThat matters because Frontier showed a personal item included, while the first checked bag was quoted in the **$50–$120** range. So a $196 JAX fare isn't automatically better than a $257 Orlando nonstop if JAX creates another $100+ of transportation afterward.\n\nFor example, **Saturday 9/26** gives us two very different plays:\n\n- **$196 JAX** — absolute fare play.\n- **$268 MCO nonstop** — only about **$72 more**, but you're across the country in **4h24** instead of spending 8